here's how you make a cozy cone motel  inspired bacon mac and cheese cone at  home  start by rolling card stock into a cone  shape and covering in aluminum foil and  coat with a nonstick cooking spray  next roll a package of pizza dough into  a large rectangle and cut into one inch  strips  starting at the point of the cone wrap  the strips around coat with egg wash and  bake in a 425 degree oven for 12 to 15  minutes  next the mac and cheese start by cooking  a pound of pasta according to the  directions  then cook your bacon and allow it to  cool now onto the cheese sauce  start by melting a fourth a cup of  butter in a saucepan over medium heat  and then add a fourth a cup of flour and  cook until golden and smooth  then add two cups of milk and whisk  until smooth and let the mixture thicken  over medium heat add half a cup of cream  cheese allowing to melt  then eight ounces of shredded cheddar  cheese and salt and pepper to taste  stir until smooth add in your cooked  noodles and mix to combine  fill your cones with the mac and cheese  top with the bacon  and enjoy let's make some iconic disney  snacks here are my top five disney  recipes you need to make at home  the cheeseburger pods from pandora are  always one of my favorites and if you  want a good hack for this recipe you  always can use flaky biscuits from a  tube for the buns  the tachos from woody's lunchbox are  always a fan favorite i mean who doesn't  love  chili over tater tots i mean potato  barrels if you've ever been to ohana you  know how good the bread pudding is  it's easier to make at home than you  would expect and you get to flambe which  sounds scary but i swear it's not  i'm telling you now if the spring roll  cart in magic kingdom is open you best  believe you can find me there  i'm making the pepperoni ones but i also  have the recipe for the cheeseburger  ones so take your pick on what you like  they come together really quick and you  also can make these in the airfryer  and finally my favorite snack slash meal  in all of disney world i have recipe  tested this one  so many times and i think i have come  close to perfection to making toronto  wrap at home so check it out  here's how you make the cheddar cheese  soup from lace ellie and epcot  this recipe is pretty simple we're  starting off by frying up some bacon and  into that we're adding celery and red  onion once that's cooked we're gonna add  in some flour for thickness  as always the full recipe will be posted  over on my instagram  then it's just a process we're adding  some chicken stock letting that simmer  i know that lace ellie is technically a  steakhouse but i think this is probably  the most famous dish on their menu once  that's simmered down and thick we're  adding some milk  the creaminess of the soup will really  come together in the last 15 minutes  simmer  you can't have cheddar cheese soup  without cheddar cheese we're adding in  eight ounces of shredded cheddar cheese  i prefer to shred my own  i just think it gives it a better  texture in the soup and then it's your  final spices which is tabasco  worcestershire salt and pepper  and it's canada so we're finishing it  off with a fourth a cup of beer  be sure to follow along for even more  disney parks recipes  do you recognize this snack let's head  over to magic kingdom and recreate one  of my all-time favorite sweet treats the  cheshire cat tail we're starting this  recipe on the stove with some milk and  vanilla and we're just heating that up  we're making an easy crumb hat the whole  recipe will be posted over on my  instagram if you have any questions  but then we're just taking eggs sugar  and corn starch giving that a mix and  then we're slowly adding the heated milk  mixture  back into the eggs just so we don't  scramble them it's called tempering  and that goes back on the stove until it  gets thick and bubbly then we're just  rolling out some frozen  puff pastry we're topping it with that  crumb pat and then we're also topping it  with mini chocolate chips  this is my favorite sweet treat in magic  kingdom it usually has its own stand but  right now you can find it at cosmic rays  then we're just folding it over  essentially like a book  and then we're just going to cut it in  one and a half inch section pop them on  a parchment lined baking sheet give them  a twist and bake them in a 400 degree  oven until golden brown  once cooled it's time to ice and that's  just powdered sugar milk and a bit of  food coloring use a spoon to drizzle and  you've got yourself a cheshire cat tale  from magic  kingdom
 

